   1          /**
   2          *   @file       calib.c
   3          *   @brief      Per-unit Si_Da calibration backed by A96L416 internal
   4          *               DataFlash. See calib.h for the design overview, the on-flash
   5          *               layout and the runtime correction formula.
   6          *
   7          *   Operational summary
   8          *   -------------------
   9          *   - calib_load()                : low-level read + validate. Populates
  10          *                                   g_calib_* or installs defaults.
  11          *   - calib_save(b, g)            : low-level erase + page write + verify.
  12          *   - calib_apply(raw)            : called on every Si_Da reading in the
  13          *                                   main loop. Applies
  14          *                                   ((raw - baseline) * gain_Q8) >> 8.
  15          *   - calib_step1_boot_led()      : STEP 1. Power-on indication, both
  16          *                                   LEDs on 0.2 s.
  17          *   - calib_erase_with_animation(): STEP 2-1. SW2 held at boot. LED G/R
  18          *                                   alternate while held; on release erase
  19          *                                   DataFlash, capture clean-air baseline,
  20          *                                   save {baseline, gain=256}.
  21          *   - calib_boot_init()           : STEP 2-2. SW2 not held - load the saved
  22          *                                   record into the RAM globals.
  23          *   - calib_run_smoke()           : STEP 3. Triggered from the main loop
  24          *                                   when SW2 is held in normal mode while a
  25          *                                   smoke calibration is still pending.
  26          *                                   place phase + 5-sample mean + gain save.
  27          */
